Probably "horrible idea"; there are enough
ascensions in the shared universe that for most of
us, sharing them across many platforms would quickly
become a situation of being unable to post any
scores to our own high score table.

One of the many reasons I started using different
names than my login-ID for characters is that with
the vanilla build and a single player, it isn't even
possible to fill the score table; 13 classes times
three high scores each is only 39 entries.

The other reason is that I quickly end up posting
enough "better" games that I can't get any newer
games onto the score table. My own "accidentally
good games" becomes, over time, a standard so high
that all games conclude with "you didn't beat your
previous score of nnn", which becomes way too
depressing to allow continued play.

Right now, things have gotten so bad, it is time for
serious consideration of discarding the high score
table, where fourteen games with five digit scores
and one anamoly game with a low six digit score,
still none of them close to ascensions, stand as
embarrassments to my usual middle four digits
scores.

Also, when I get focused on one or two classes, as
right now, wizards and rogues, the score table clots
up even more quickly, so that I can only reuse a
character name about a dozen times before I need to
invent a new one; just now "Slime Bait" is having a
fairly good wizard game.

